    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="1036" n="1018" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg1018"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24557H/5–1948: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Norway</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Huston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Oslo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-19">May 19, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    A–273. Embtel
                    115, March 11, 1947. FoMin Lange told Ambassador Bay yesterday, in reply to a
                    question, that there have been no developments whatever in the Spitsbergen
                    question since the despatch of his letter to Molotov last year conveying
                    Norway’s refusal to enter into negotiations looking to the joint defense of the
                    archipelago. Mr. Lange indicated that he considered the subject “dead”, at least
                    for the time being.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
